1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,719
Katalyst turns a plain-language intent into a verified
settlement on Portaldot.

2
00:00:05,939 --> 00:00:10,993
Today I will run one for real, live on the Portaldot V3
testnet.

3
00:00:12,243 --> 00:00:15,132
Intent in, settlement out.

4
00:00:15,352 --> 00:00:24,551
You say what you want. GenLayer validators agree on the route.
A vault on Portaldot checks that route and pays the pools.

5
00:00:24,771 --> 00:00:29,480
The figures on this page are read straight from the vault's
events on Portaldot.

6
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:37,429
In the app, I describe my intent: maximize yield, but only
A-Tier carbon pools.

7
00:00:37,649 --> 00:00:42,874
Before depositing anything, I can ask the validators for a
free preview.

8
00:00:43,094 --> 00:00:49,073
Two pools qualify, and the lower rated pool is excluded, with
the reason shown.

9
00:00:50,123 --> 00:00:57,462
I lock the route, so the vault pays exactly this route or
nothing, and deposit three tenths of a testnet POT.

10
00:00:57,682 --> 00:01:02,081
This is a real transaction, signed and sent to Portaldot.

11
00:01:03,723 --> 00:01:09,192
Now GenLayer's validators reach consensus. Most of them agree.

12
00:01:09,412 --> 00:01:14,301
The relayer proposes the route to the vault, but cannot move
funds yet.

13
00:01:14,521 --> 00:01:22,935
A safety delay starts. The vault owner can veto during it, and
a guardian checks the route against the validators' verdict.

14
00:01:23,155 --> 00:01:27,110
When the delay ends, the vault settles on Portaldot.

15
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:34,404
Here is that settlement block in Portaldot's own explorer.

16
00:01:34,624 --> 00:01:41,933
It is a real Ethereum style transaction, executed on the
Portaldot testnet and sent to our vault contract.

17
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:48,865
Now the part that matters most. Do not trust us, verify.

18
00:01:49,085 --> 00:02:00,973
This page rebuilds the story from Portaldot events and the
validators' own records: the deposit, the consensus, the route
that was paid, the fee, the route lock and the safety delay.

19
00:02:01,193 --> 00:02:03,338
Every check passes.

20
00:02:04,495 --> 00:02:11,574
We also tested a failure on testnet. A relayer proposed a
route the validators never chose.

21
00:02:11,794 --> 00:02:18,333
The guardian caught it during the delay, the owner vetoed it,
and the depositor got every token back.

22
00:02:18,553 --> 00:02:22,742
Verify marks it: the safety delay caught a bad route.

23
00:02:24,005 --> 00:02:31,934
The vault's rules, its fee, cap, timeout and delay, are fixed
at deployment. Nobody can change them.

24
00:02:33,175 --> 00:02:39,814
Katalyst. GenLayer decides, Portaldot settles, and anyone can
verify.

25
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:47,678
It is live on testnet today and open source. Next come an
audit, a relayer quorum, and mainnet.
